      "content": "thanks for the help!! that's actually really useful for my outline.\n\ni was looking at the split you made, and it's interesting how the 'architects' side is almost entirely about formal legal and logical systems that we see in the modern west, while the 'empirical' side is where all the actual physical inventions and mathematical tools end up. \n\nit makes me wonder though—if the 'structural' side is what actually dictates how a society operates and thinks, doesn't that imply that the cultures in the 'empirical' bucket were essentially just supplying the raw materials or tools for the 'architects' to build with? like, is the real 'logic' of civilization found in the structural bucket, and the other stuff is just... a collection of useful discoveries?",
